# Full passwordless sudo for the box's own user.
#
# Owner's call, 2026-10-09: the project is free and open source, and somebody who owns the hardware
# should be able to change it without a password they were never told. The narrow NOPASSWD rules
# beside this one stay as they are - they document what the SERVER is allowed to do, which is worth
# keeping explicit even when this rule makes them redundant.
#
# What keeps this reasonable rather than reckless:
#   - sshd is DISABLED in the shipped image. There is no remote login to escalate from unless the
#     builder turns it on in Imager, at which point they have chosen it and set their own password.
#   - The account password is per-box: whatever the builder typed into Imager, or a random one
#     nobody ever learns. There is no shared default to publish.
#   - Anyone physically holding the box can pull the card and edit it anyway.
#
# It also means provisioning, over-the-air updates and check-drift.sh never need a password after
# the first run, which removes the prompt that made the build un-runnable unattended.
__BOX_USER__ ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL
